{# The public site: homepage, marketing pages, docs and blog.

   These used to render inside the app shell, which meant every visitor to
   the front page downloaded the whole budgeting app -- the store, its 13
   slices, and the per-route view scripts -- to read a paragraph. They also
   got a sidebar of Balances for a profile they may not have.

   Alpine IS still loaded, because partials/header.njk and
   partials/theme-picker.njk are Alpine components and render on every page.
   The store is not: every $store reference in header.njk sits inside its
   `isApp` branch. #}

{% extends "layouts/base.njk" %}

{% block bodyClass %}layout-marketing{% endblock %}

{% block scripts %}
  <script src="/assets/js/vendor/alpine.min.js" defer></script>
  {# instant.page prefetches links on hover/touch. Marketing only. #}
  <script src="/assets/js/vendor/instantpage.min.js" type="module" defer></script>
{% endblock %}
